  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1226 PM CDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nBroad troughing is centered to our east and northeast putting\nthe area in a moderate northwesterly flow aloft. A jet max works\nin on the backside of this trough through Sunday morning keeping\nit roughly in place. There is a small window for thundershowers\nacross parts of SEMO Saturday afternoon but the chances are low\n(15%).\n\nBy Monday that trough works east far enough to allow the heat\nand humidity to start to creep back into the area. This opens\nthe potential again for daily mainly afternoon showers and\nthunderstorms with fairly low coverage overall (15-30%). The\nbest chance for activity for now looks to be Wednesday afternoon\nand evening when a little sharper shortwave pushes through. If \nany severe weather threat is to emerge in the next 7 days it \nlooks like this could be the period. If the trough position and \nshear/instability remain consistent we might be able to start \nmessaging a threat, but for now it appears too low\npredictability/threat for much concern.",
